  "summary_md": "Soft housing turnover continues to weigh on the sector, with persistent top-line pressure at ETD, BSET, and HOFT contrasting against resilient share gains and product-driven growth at FLXS and LCUT. Tariffs remain a messy cross-current—temporarily lifting margins at COOK and HBB while dampening orders elsewhere—leaving demand recovery uneven and fragile.\n\nStrategic extremes define this batch. AMWD’s pending MasterBrand acquisition creates genuine integration uncertainty even as operational momentum improves, while SNBR faces an acute balance-sheet crisis and going-concern warning that completely overshadows its product reboot. A striking wave of transformation is unfolding among smaller names: XWIN is pivoting from furniture design into an AI platform with SpaceX-linked exposure, ATER is exiting e-commerce entirely for critical-mineral exploration, and MWYN is promoting an AI infrastructure narrative—all unproven, high-risk shifts. NCL’s activist pact and guidance reset add another layer of strategic flux, making this a batch where existential repositioning and financial risk demand the most scrutiny.",
